WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:02.480
““Summerhall.”

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.540
The word was fraught with doom”.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:10.630
It ended at Summerhall, with “sorcery, fire,
and grief”.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:15.290
The “tragedy at Summerhall” was a mysterious
disaster that happened forty years before

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:17.800
the main story of Game of Thrones.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:24.740
It was a fire that killed a king, and birthed
a prince, and is tied to dragons, magic, prophecy,

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:26.990
and the destiny of Westeros.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.070
So what happened at Summerhall?

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:35.039
A hundred years ago, King Daeron Targaryen
peacefully unified Dorne with the rest of

00:00:35.039 --> 00:00:36.129
Westeros.

00:00:36.129 --> 00:00:41.320
To celebrate, he built a castle called Summerhall,
near the borders of the Reach, stormlands,

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.539
and Dorne.

00:00:42.539 --> 00:00:47.749
It was a “lightly fortified” castle, more
of a “palace” – used as a home for Targaryen

00:00:47.749 --> 00:00:48.749
princes.

00:00:48.749 --> 00:00:53.820
In the time of the Dunk and Egg stories, Daeron’s
son Maekar and some of his family lived there.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.390
And eventually, Maekar’s son Aegon, or Egg,
became king.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:03.090
In his adventures with Dunk, Egg learned to
respect the smallfolk – the.. peasants,

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:07.320
or common people – and to care for the “poor
and weak”.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:12.861
So as king, Egg made laws to help the smallfolk,
giving them new rights and protections, and

00:01:12.861 --> 00:01:15.220
limiting the power of the lords.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:21.430
Many lords hated this, and some rebelled against
him, so Egg spent much of his reign fighting

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:23.330
rebellions [including a rebellion by the Laughing
Storm, Lyonel Baratheon!].

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:24.980
Even Egg’s children were rebellious.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:29.550
Egg and his wife Betha arranged marriages
for their kids that would help build alliances

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:35.100
with other powerful houses, but their sons
refused these arranged marriages.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:40.570
Egg’s eldest son and heir Prince Duncan
gave up his claim to the throne and married

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:43.960
a mysterious common woman called Jenny of
Oldstones.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:49.780
Egg’s son Jaehaerys and daughter Shaera
fell in love with each other, and got married.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:55.270
They had two kids, Aerys and Rhaella, who
also married each other and had kids, which

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:57.390
is, like, super.. double.. incest.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:01.330
That’s where Rhaegar Viserys and Daenerys
come from.

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:07.390
Egg’s youngest son Daeron was meant to marry
a young Olenna Redwyne, the Queen of Thorns.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:12.349
But Daeron refused the marriage, and instead
had a relationship with a knight called Ser

00:02:12.349 --> 00:02:15.519
Jeremy, before they died together in a battle.

00:02:15.519 --> 00:02:19.999
Since Prince Duncan broke a betrothal with
a Baratheon, his sister Rhaelle married a

00:02:19.999 --> 00:02:25.719
Baratheon instead – which led to birth of
Robert Baratheon, who would later overthrow

00:02:25.719 --> 00:02:27.379
the Targaryens.

00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:33.310
So King Egg was frustrated with his disobedient
children, and rebellious lords, and he also

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:38.460
faced the threat of the Blackfyres – he
defeated the Fourth Blackfyre Rebellion, but

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:43.769
a fifth rebellion loomed, with Maelys the
Monstrous and the Ninepenny Kings gathering

00:02:43.769 --> 00:02:45.250
in the east.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:50.980
All Egg wanted was to bring “peace and prosperity
and justice” to Westeros, but he couldn’t

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:55.220
do it when everyone fought against him, and
forced him to compromise.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:03:01.010
Egg came to believe that the only way he could
get enough power to bring justice to the realm

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:03.330
was with dragons.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:08.329
For the first hundred years of their dynasty,
the Targaryens could crush any enemy with

00:03:08.329 --> 00:03:09.379
their dragons.

00:03:09.379 --> 00:03:14.480
But after the Targaryen civil war, the Dance
of the Dragons, the dragons went extinct,

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.829
and the Targaryens weren’t as powerful.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:21.739
They still had dragon eggs, and they tried
everything to make them hatch – King Aegon

00:03:21.739 --> 00:03:28.080
the Third got nine mages to work spells over
the eggs, Baelor the Blessed prayed over the

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:34.239
eggs, maesters pored over the eggs, Egg’s
brother Aerion drank wildfire to transform

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:38.439
himself into a dragon – but they all failed.

00:03:38.439 --> 00:03:43.569
Every time the Targaryens tried to hatch dragons,
they just “made fools of themselves, or

00:03:43.569 --> 00:03:45.030
corpses”.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:50.290
But still – Egg’s brother Daeron, and
his uncle Aerys, even Daemon Blackfyre the

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:57.110
Second all said that dragons would return
– they saw it in prophetic dreams, and read

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:59.069
of it in prophecy.

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:03.300
Soon, King Egg too dreamed of dragons.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:09.090
He became obsessed with ancient Valyrian dragon
lore, sending people searching as far east

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:12.439
as Asshai for lost books and knowledge on
dragon breeding.

00:04:12.439 --> 00:04:18.590
He was desperate for the power that he believed
could bring peace to Westeros.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:23.190
And this dream of dragons led to the tragedy
at Summerhall.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:28.780
The books only give us tiny hints of information
what happened, but here’s what we know – King

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:34.250
Egg gathered his family together, to celebrate
the pregnancy of his granddaughter Rhaella.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:40.990
And there, King Egg performed some kind of
ritual involving seven dragon eggs, pyromancers,

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:42.390
and wild fire.

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:46.020
The fire got out of control, and people died.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:48.910
The books don’t actually say who died.

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:55.150
But it’s implied, and the official app confirms,
that King Egg, his son Duncan, and his Kingsguard

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:57.800
Dunk died in the fire.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:03.330
Rhaella survived, and as Summerhall burned,
she gave birth to Prince Rhaegar.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:08.539
The book hints that Dunk saved people from
the fire before he died, so maybe Dunk saved

00:05:08.539 --> 00:05:10.440
Rhaella and Rhaegar.

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:15.580
Back in The Hedge Knight, Dunk thinks that
the realm might need his foot one day – so

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:19.520
maybe he.. kicks down a door to save the princess.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:24.900
Then goes back into the fire to save King
Egg, and dies with him, perhaps.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:29.080
It sounds like Jenny of Oldstones may have
died in the fire.

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:34.470
And possibly Queen Betha, and Egg’s sisters
and their families, and Egg’s brothers’

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:35.470
children.

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:40.990
Summerhall explains why there are so few Targaryens
left in the story – this disaster wiped

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:43.629
out a generation of them.

00:05:43.629 --> 00:05:46.090
It was a catastrophe for the royal family.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:49.480
So what caused this fire?

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:55.750
We know King Egg was trying to hatch dragons
– he had seven dragon eggs and “wild fire”.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:59.940
So maybe he thought the eggs would hatch if
he put them in a really hot fire.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:01.840
Which isn’t a bad idea.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:06.860
The Targaryens used to hatch their dragon
eggs in the fires of the volcanic island Dragonstone

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:10.889
– some said that the eggs needed that heat
to hatch.

00:06:10.889 --> 00:06:14.939
So maybe King Egg was just cooking up some
googs, and things got out of hand.

00:06:14.939 --> 00:06:20.780
Cause Egg was using wildfire, with the pyromancers
of the Alchemists’ Guild.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:26.879
And wildfire is super dangerous, it can easily
get out of control – “any little mistake

00:06:26.879 --> 00:06:29.280
can bring catastrophe”.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:35.650
In Book 2, we learn that the pyromancers make
wildfire in rooms rigged with sand held above,

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:41.229
so if the wildfire gets out of control, the
sand falls down and smothers the flame – and

00:06:41.229 --> 00:06:44.080
kills any people inside.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:51.130
And in Dunk &amp; Egg, Dunk has a dream where
he and Egg are suffocated in sand.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:58.620
So some fans think this sand system was set
up at Summerhall, and killed Dunk and Egg.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:03.740
Whatever the details, playing with fire is
dangerous, so maybe Summerhall was just a

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:05.569
terrible accident.

00:07:05.569 --> 00:07:11.009
But if that’s true, why all the secrecy
and mystery around Summerhall?

00:07:11.009 --> 00:07:16.629
The survivors would not speak of what happened,
and this part of the worldbook is ‘blotted

00:07:16.629 --> 00:07:20.520
out by ink’ so we can’t see the details
of what happened.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:23.770
What’s the author hiding here?

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:27.599
There are theories that Summerhall was not
an accident.

00:07:27.599 --> 00:07:31.000
That death was part of the plan.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:38.189
Cause in this story, human sacrifice has magical
power – “Only death can pay for life”,

00:07:38.189 --> 00:07:41.830
and “A great gift requires” “great sacrifice”.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:47.949
Like, Daenerys tries putting her dragon eggs
in a fire, and that doesn’t make them hatch.

00:07:47.949 --> 00:07:54.009
They hatch when she burns Mirri Maz Duur and
the body of Khal Drogo in a big funeral pyre

00:07:54.009 --> 00:07:55.540
with her eggs.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:08:01.400
That sacrifice hatches her dragons, cause
“Only death can pay for life”.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:07.919
In Book 2, Melisandre tries to wake a dragon
by burning a bastard son of King Robert.

00:08:07.919 --> 00:08:13.169
She says “Only a king’s blood can wake
the stone dragon”.

00:08:13.169 --> 00:08:18.210
By ‘stone dragon’, she seems to think
she can transform the stone dragon statues

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:24.780
on Dragonstone into living dragons, but ‘stone
dragons’ can also refer to dragon eggs that

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:27.939
have petrified into stone over time.

00:08:27.939 --> 00:08:34.760
The point is, we’ve twice seen the idea
that human sacrifice in a fire can wake dragons.

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:41.469
So maybe the fire at Summerhall was a sacrifice
to hatch dragon eggs, and King Egg deliberately

00:08:41.469 --> 00:08:43.229
burned people.

00:08:43.229 --> 00:08:48.250
Since “king’s blood” has special power
to wake dragons, King Egg might’ve sacrificed

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:52.510
himself, walking into the fire like Daenerys.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:58.329
In Book 5, Melisandre wants to sacrifice a
king, and then his son, so that “both die

00:08:58.329 --> 00:09:03.220
kings” to maximise the magical power to
“wake the dragon”.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:09.149
Maybe King Egg tried the same thing, burning
himself and then his son Duncan.

00:09:09.149 --> 00:09:14.260
Or since Duncan abdicated, he could’ve tried
to burn Jaehaerys instead.

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:20.310
Maybe Egg tried to sacrifice Rhaella, and
her unborn child Rhaegar, as the ultimate

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:26.890
terrible sacrifice to wake the dragons, but
Dunk intervened and stopped him.

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:33.000
We can only speculate about the details, but
given what we know about magic and sacrifice

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:39.070
and dragons, Summerhall looks a lot like a
magic sacrifice to hatch dragons.

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:45.470
But is Egg the kind of person who would burn
his own family alive?

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:50.769
In the Dunk &amp; Egg stories, Egg is a sweet
kid, he’s not mad or cruel.

00:09:50.769 --> 00:09:54.600
He only occasionally gets angry and Targaryeny.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:58.310
But being king changes people.

00:09:58.310 --> 00:10:01.029
You have to be ruthless to rule.

00:10:01.029 --> 00:10:06.180
When Egg became king, his brother Aemon told
him that “It takes a man to rule.

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:08.680
An Aegon, not an Egg”.

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:13.740
“Kill the boy within you”, “and let
the man be born”.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:21.890
Maybe King Egg tried to “kill the boy”
at Summerhall, to let dragons be born.

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:28.480
It’s a similar story to Stannis, a king
with good intentions who burns people alive

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.070
as sacrifices.

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:35.820
He argues that the sacrifice of one child
is worth it if it saves the kingdom.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:38.720
Maybe King Egg thought the same thing.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:44.019
When Stannis considers burning Mance and his
baby to wake a dragon, Aemon says “There

00:10:44.019 --> 00:10:49.850
is power in a king’s blood” “and better
men than Stannis have done worse things than

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:51.139
this”.

00:10:51.139 --> 00:10:57.670
Maybe Aemon is talking about his brother Egg,
a good man who did a terrible thing, sacrificing

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:01.540
his family to wake dragons for the realm.

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:07.399
But what could’ve convinced Egg that a magic
sacrifice would work?

00:11:07.399 --> 00:11:11.029
King Egg’s family was really into prophecy.

00:11:11.029 --> 00:11:17.170
Prince Duncan’s wife, Jenny of Oldstones,
brought a “woods witch” to court – a

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:20.899
“dwarfish” “albino” woman who was
connected to the magic of the old gods.

00:11:20.899 --> 00:11:24.850
We meet this this witch forty years later
in the main series, where she’s called the

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:26.810
ghost of High Heart.

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:32.260
And she has accurate visions of the future,
foreseeing the Red Wedding, and Joffrey’s

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:34.130
poisoning, before they happen.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:38.290
So this witch is legit – she can see the
future.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:44.270
And she was influential in King Egg’s court
– Prince Aerys and Rhaella got married because

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:50.360
this witch said that the prince that was promised,
or Azor Ahai, would be born of their line.

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:56.220
Which means that Daenerys or Jon might be
the prophesied heroes to save the world from

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:57.990
the white walkers.

00:11:57.990 --> 00:12:03.120
Maybe that’s why Prince Duncan abdicated
the Throne – so his nephew Aerys, and the

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:07.050
line of Azor Ahai, would inherit the Throne
instead.

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:11.769
Some fans suspect that Bloodraven, also connected
to the old gods, had something to do with

00:12:11.769 --> 00:12:12.769
this.

00:12:12.769 --> 00:12:17.800
So.. that’s a whole thing, but we also know
that Egg’s brother Aemon and his uncle Aerys

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:23.470
were also interested in prophecy, as well
as Daeron with his dragon dreams, and Aerion

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.470
with his delusions.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:31.220
So just like your auntie who’s like a little
bit too into astrology, King Egg’s family

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:35.730
were heavily influenced by prophecies and
dreams of the future.

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:42.220
So maybe Egg did Summerhall because he or
the ghost of High Heart or Daeron, had a prophetic

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:46.880
dream that dragons would hatch from fire at
Summerhall.

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:53.180
Problem is, relying on prophecy in this story
is dangerous – “Prophecy will bite your

00:12:53.180 --> 00:12:56.240
prick off every time”.

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:59.980
Many characters have dreams of the future,
especially Targaryens.

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:06.160
And especially dreams about terrible destructive
events, like the Doom of Valyria.. and the

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:12.589
Red Wedding – the ghost of High Heart, Daenerys,
Patchface, even Theon all have dreams and

00:13:12.589 --> 00:13:15.820
visions of the Red Wedding before it happens.

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:21.279
But dreams of the future are often symbolic
and abstract, and are often misinterpreted

00:13:21.279 --> 00:13:26.589
by the dreamer – like, Melisandre constantly
misinterprets her visions to convince herself

00:13:26.589 --> 00:13:29.110
that Stannis is the prophesied hero.

00:13:29.110 --> 00:13:34.490
She once has a vision of Alys Karstark and
convinces herself it's Arya Stark.

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:40.340
The visions are true, but she twists the meaning
to see what she wants to see.

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:44.910
Misinterpreting a dream can lead to a character’s
downfall – like, in The Mystery Knight,

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:50.780
Daemon dreams of a hatching dragon, so he
thinks he’ll get a dragon and win the Throne,

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:54.440
but he misinterpreted the dream, so Daemon
fails.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:14:00.730
Aemon says that his brothers Egg Daeron and
Aerion were all killed by their dreams of

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:01.730
dragons.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:06.370
Cause Aerion dreamed of transforming into
a dragon by drinking wildfire.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:10.560
Daeron’s dragon dreams drove him to self-destructive
drinking.

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:14.990
Maybe Egg’s dragon dreams killed him because,
like Daemon and Melisandre and others, he

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:21.529
misinterpreted his visions, and saw what he
wanted to see YouTuber JoeMagician argues

00:14:21.529 --> 00:14:27.069
that Egg may have had visions of the future
of Daenerys hatching dragons from fire, and

00:14:27.069 --> 00:14:32.170
Summerhall was Egg’s attempt to recreate
this dream, thinking that the vision was about

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:33.459
him.

00:14:33.459 --> 00:14:38.230
Because the sacrifices at Summerhall mirror
the sacrifices at Daenerys’ fire – King

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:43.640
Egg parallels Khal Drogo, cause a Khal is
symbolically like a king.

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:47.510
Princess Rhaella Targaryen mirrors Princess
Daenerys Targaryen.

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:53.250
And Rhaella’s baby Rhaegar mirrors Daenerys’
baby Rhaego, who dies shortly before this

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:54.740
funeral pyre.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:59.480
The witch Mirri Maz Duur mirrors the woods
witch, the ghost of High Heart.

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:05.490
Maybe through the symbolic language of prophetic
dreams, Egg saw a king and a princess and

00:15:05.490 --> 00:15:11.160
a baby and witch burning on a fire, and saw
dragons hatching from the ashes.

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:16.960
He thought this was his destiny, and tried
to make it happen by burning himself and his

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:23.819
family, to hatch dragons and save the realm,
tragically misled by prophecy like so many

00:15:23.819 --> 00:15:25.940
others before him.

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:31.120
JoeMagician speculates that other Targaryens
might also have had the same dream of Daenerys’s

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:32.120
fire.

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:36.400
Mad King Aerys tried to burn King’s Landing
in a great “funeral pyre”, thinking he

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:42.180
would rise again as a dragon – which sounds
a lot like Daenerys rising from her funeral

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:44.459
pyre with dragons.

00:15:44.459 --> 00:15:49.519
Aerion might’ve had the same dream to convince
him that fire would make him a dragon.

00:15:49.519 --> 00:15:54.330
All these Targaryens destroyed themselves
thinking that fire would give them dragons

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:58.949
– maybe they all dreamed of Daenerys.

00:15:58.949 --> 00:16:05.910
Cause the rebirth of dragons is a powerfully
significant magical event, so just like the

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:11.629
Doom of Valyria and the Red Wedding – and
Euron Greyjoy’s coming apocalypse – it

00:16:11.629 --> 00:16:17.180
sent shockwaves through time, ripples in the
dreamscape, bringing prophetic visions to

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:24.149
sensitive individuals, and causing generations
of Targaryen madness and fiery catastrophe.

00:16:24.149 --> 00:16:26.850
That’s one theory, anyway.

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:29.990
We don’t know if King Egg had visions of
the future.

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:34.269
We don’t even know for sure if he deliberately
sacrificed people.

00:16:34.269 --> 00:16:38.209
But whatever he did to hatch dragons, it failed.

00:16:38.209 --> 00:16:41.569
And House Targaryen was left weaker than before.

00:16:41.569 --> 00:16:47.660
Egg’s sickly second son Jaehaerys inherited
the Throne, then came King Aerys, who was

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:53.629
mad, possibly because of the fire and trauma
of Summerhall, then the Targaryens were overthrown

00:16:53.629 --> 00:16:55.279
in Robert’s Rebellion.

00:16:55.279 --> 00:17:02.129
So was Summerhall just a giant meaningless
fuckup that led to the end of the Targaryens?

00:17:02.129 --> 00:17:07.470
Or did this death and disaster birth some
hope?

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:12.370
In Dunk &amp; Egg, Egg’s brother Daeron has
a dream of a dragon dying.

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:17.559
But in the end, it’s not a literal dragon
that dies, it’s a metaphorical dragon, Baelor

00:17:17.559 --> 00:17:18.959
Targaryen.

00:17:18.959 --> 00:17:23.140
Then in The Mystery Knight, Daemon Blackfyre
has a dream that a dragon will hatch from

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.270
an egg.

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:28.929
But in the end, it’s not a literal dragon
that hatches, it’s a metaphor for Egg becoming

00:17:28.929 --> 00:17:31.850
a more confident Targaryen prince.

00:17:31.850 --> 00:17:37.490
So in prophetic dreams, a dragon doesn’t
always mean a literal dragon, it can mean

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:38.980
a Targaryen.

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:44.600
And in the same way, the fire at Summerhall
didn’t hatch a literal dragon, but it did

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:50.480
lead to the birth of Rhaegar Targaryen, who
is sometimes called a “dragon”.

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:56.309
So in a way, King Egg succeeded in hatching
a dragon at Summerhall – just not in the

00:17:56.309 --> 00:17:58.919
way he expected.

00:17:58.919 --> 00:18:04.640
Author George Martin says he likes prophecies
that come true, but in an unexpected way.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:11.280
And even though Summerhall was a disaster,
that sacrifice at the birth of Rhaegar might’ve

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:15.549
set events in motion for Westeros to be saved.

00:18:15.549 --> 00:18:18.840
Like his ancestors, Rhaegar was very into
prophecy.

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:24.260
At one point, he and Aemon believed that Rhaegar
was the prince that was promised, or Azor

00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:25.260
Ahai.

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:30.350
Cause the hero is prophesied to be born “amidst
smoke and salt”.

00:18:30.350 --> 00:18:35.510
Aemon said the smoke was from the fire at
Summerhall, and the salt was from the tears

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:37.900
shed for the people who died there.

00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:44.490
So maybe the tragedy at Summerhall fulfilled
the prophecy to make Rhaegar the hero to save

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:45.490
the world.

00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:48.440
Of course, Rhaegar did not save the world.

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:50.840
He got killed by Robert Baratheon.

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:57.169
But Rhaegar did probably father Jon Snow,
who along with Daenerys, probably will be

00:18:57.169 --> 00:19:00.500
the heroes who’ll save the world from the
white walkers.

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:06.940
By some interpretations, Rhaegar was the hero
Azor Ahai, but Jon and Daenerys and her dragons

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:13.309
are Lightbringer, the fiery sword that will
defeat the darkness, born of sacrifice.

00:19:13.309 --> 00:19:19.450
So the prophecy works out –the tragedy at
Summerhall might have been a necessary sacrifice

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:23.140
to birth the heroes who’ll save Westeros.

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:28.260
Death did pay for life, though the price was
terrible.

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:32.080
Rhaegar was “haunted” by the tragedy of
Summerhall.

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:37.790
“He was born in grief”, “and that shadow
hung over him all his days”.

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:43.669
He would go alone to the ruins of Summerhall,
his birthplace, and write sad songs of sorrow

00:19:43.669 --> 00:19:45.220
and death.

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:50.289
Some fans speculate that he may have met the
ghost of High Heart at Summerhall, and sang

00:19:50.289 --> 00:19:53.350
her songs in return for prophetic visions.

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:58.020
Cause in Book 3, the ghost wants music in
return for her dreams.

00:19:58.020 --> 00:20:04.730
And she always asks for the same song – Jenny’s
song, that sad, longing song that Podrick

00:20:04.730 --> 00:20:06.540
sings in the tv show.

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:12.080
The song is about the ghost’s friend Jenny
of Oldstones, and she weeps as she listens

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:16.309
– she says she “gorged on grief at Summerhall”.

00:20:16.309 --> 00:20:21.520
If the ghost’s prophecies are what convinced
Egg to burn Summerhall, maybe the ghost feels

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:24.220
guilt as well as grief.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:29.380
Some fans speculate that Rhaegar wrote Jenny’s
song for the ghost of High Heart.

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:34.760
Rhaegar seemed to share that same sense of
sadness and doom.

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:41.070
Maybe he understood that the tragedy at Summerhall
was a sacrifice, a terrible price to pay for

00:20:41.070 --> 00:20:43.960
life in Westeros.

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:46.630
There are other theories about Summerhall.

00:20:46.630 --> 00:20:51.880
Like maybe there was a conspiracy, and some
other faction caused the disaster.

00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:58.220
After all, King Egg had many powerful enemies,
like all the lords who hated his laws, who

00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:01.870
viewed him as a blood-handed tyrant.

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:06.990
Maybe they chucked some extra wildfire into
the mix to kill King Egg.

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:13.059
In Book 4, Marwyn the Mage says that the maesters
have a conspiracy against magic, Targaryens

00:21:13.059 --> 00:21:14.490
and dragons.

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:19.020
He claims that the maesters somehow caused
the extinction of the dragons in the first

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:20.020
place.

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:24.690
We know that maesters “pored” over the
remaining dragon eggs – maybe they poisoned

00:21:24.690 --> 00:21:27.450
the eggs, to stop them from hatching.

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:32.200
Then when King Egg tried to bring back the
dragons, maybe the maesters made sure it failed,

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:36.110
and blew up the Targaryens once and for all.

00:21:36.110 --> 00:21:41.380
The Grand Maester at the time was a young
Pycelle, and we know he’s not trustworthy

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:48.530
– he betrayed Mad King Aerys, he betrayed
Jon Arryn, maybe he betrayed King Egg too.

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:53.470
At the time, a young Tywin Lannister was a
cupbearer to King Egg.

00:21:53.470 --> 00:21:58.460
And Tywin would’ve hated Egg’s pro-peasant
laws as much as anyone.

00:21:58.460 --> 00:22:03.640
And Pycelle is loyal to Tywin – so maybe
these guys worked together to make sure the

00:22:03.640 --> 00:22:10.300
Summerhall fire killed Egg – a cheeky bit
of regicide to kick off their life-long alliance.

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:13.419
And maybe a young Mad Aerys was in on it.

00:22:13.419 --> 00:22:16.240
He and Tywin were childhood friends.

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:20.690
And King Egg’s death did move Aerys closer
to inheriting the Throne.

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:26.990
Each one of this trio of villainous teenagers
had potential motives to kill Egg, and they

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:29.790
were all in the king’s inner circle.

00:22:29.790 --> 00:22:33.460
Maybe they worked together to cause Summerhall.

00:22:33.460 --> 00:22:35.710
Or maybe the Faceless Men did it.

00:22:35.710 --> 00:22:40.860
It’s hinted that the Faceless Men caused
the fiery Doom of Valyria, which killed most

00:22:40.860 --> 00:22:45.929
of the dragonlords four hundred years ago
– maybe they also caused the fiery Summerhall

00:22:45.929 --> 00:22:50.380
which killed most of the Targaryens, to stop
the return of dragons.

00:22:50.380 --> 00:22:55.320
The Faceless Men are master assassins who
“take great care to make their killings”

00:22:55.320 --> 00:23:00.860
look like “natural deaths” – maybe the
Faceless Men used the Summerhall fire to hide

00:23:00.860 --> 00:23:02.400
their murder.

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:07.500
Maybe the Faceless Men were hired by Maelys
Blackfyre and the Ninepenny Kings.

00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:12.500
They wanted King Egg’s throne, and they
certainly didn’t want him to get dragons.

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:16.680
Or maybe Bloodraven did it, working with the
ghost of High Heart.

00:23:16.680 --> 00:23:20.240
They’re both connected to the magic of the
old gods.

00:23:20.240 --> 00:23:25.250
Maybe Bloodraven sent the ghost her prophetic
dreams, and made Summerhall happen, cause

00:23:25.250 --> 00:23:29.929
he wanted a sacrifice to make Rhaegar Azor
Ahai, or cause he wanted to ensure that the

00:23:29.929 --> 00:23:32.980
line of Azor Ahai would inherit the Throne.

00:23:32.980 --> 00:23:37.660
Bloodraven has repeatedly shown that he’s
willing to kill his relatives for the sake

00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:40.450
of the Targaryen bloodline.

00:23:40.450 --> 00:23:46.000
Maybe Bloodraven’s lover Shiera Seastar
started the fire, and now she wears the mask

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:50.610
of Quaithe to hide her arson-burned face.

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:57.730
Or maybe it was Daario disguised as Ser Pounce
with a book of matches and a can of gasoline.

00:23:57.730 --> 00:23:59.870
We can speculate all day.

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:05.419
There’s lots of possibilities for elaborate
conspiracies, but there’s little evidence

00:24:05.419 --> 00:24:07.159
in the books.

00:24:07.159 --> 00:24:13.080
Summerhall is the end of the story of Dunk
and Egg, it might be the final novella in

00:24:13.080 --> 00:24:14.080
their series.

00:24:14.080 --> 00:24:19.059
So you’d think the tragedy at Summerhall
will be about be about their character arcs,

00:24:19.059 --> 00:24:20.630
their choices.

00:24:20.630 --> 00:24:25.240
Author George Martin writes about “the human
heart in conflict with itself”.

00:24:25.240 --> 00:24:30.580
Like Jon Snow’s conflict between his love
for Ygritte and his duty to the Watch.

00:24:30.580 --> 00:24:36.970
George Martin loves this kind of tragic heart-wrenching
drama, and you can imagine something similar

00:24:36.970 --> 00:24:38.410
at Summerhall.

00:24:38.410 --> 00:24:43.590
Like Egg would be conflicted between his love
for his family, and the need for sacrifice

00:24:43.590 --> 00:24:46.080
to wake dragons for the realm.

00:24:46.080 --> 00:24:51.690
And Dunk would be conflicted between his loyalty
to Egg and his duty as a knight to protect

00:24:51.690 --> 00:24:52.870
the innocent.

00:24:52.870 --> 00:24:58.470
They could have a dramatic confrontation amidst
the flames of Summerhall, the two friends

00:24:58.470 --> 00:25:04.800
divided in the end like Frodo and Sam on Mount
Doom, with Dunk desperately trying to stop

00:25:04.800 --> 00:25:09.450
Egg from sacrificing innocent lives to the
fire.

00:25:09.450 --> 00:25:15.710
Maybe in the end, Dunk has to kill Egg, to
stop the burning, like Jaime and Aerys years

00:25:15.710 --> 00:25:16.710
later.

00:25:16.710 --> 00:25:17.710
[It’s like poetry it rhymes].

00:25:17.710 --> 00:25:23.220
That kind of personal drama at Summerhall
could give a fitting and emotionally devastating

00:25:23.220 --> 00:25:26.280
end to The Tales of Dunk and Egg.

00:25:26.280 --> 00:25:32.289
While making the tragedy really about a maester
conspiracy or the Faceless Men instead might

00:25:32.289 --> 00:25:39.090
undermine the personal, emotional climax of
Dunk and Egg’s story.

00:25:39.090 --> 00:25:44.740
Ultimately, dragons and magic are a metaphor
for power and ambition, and the dangers of

00:25:44.740 --> 00:25:46.860
power and ambition.

00:25:46.860 --> 00:25:53.559
Like Icarus flying to the sun, too much ambition
can get you burned and cause your downfall.

00:25:53.559 --> 00:25:56.850
And that’s what the Targaryens are all about.

00:25:56.850 --> 00:26:03.380
Their ambition and powerlust forged the Seven
Kingdoms into a united realm – but they

00:26:03.380 --> 00:26:08.799
also burned thousands of people in wars and
disasters and madness.

00:26:08.799 --> 00:26:15.220
Summerhall is a warning against the dangers
of power, ambition, and dreams, showing how

00:26:15.220 --> 00:26:22.510
even a good king like Egg, or Stannis, or
Daenerys, with the best intentions, can ultimately,

00:26:22.510 --> 00:26:26.270
tragically, end in atrocity.

00:26:26.270 --> 00:26:29.330
Fire can be the power to do great things.

00:26:29.330 --> 00:26:35.789
But “Too much light can hurt the eyes”,
and “fire burns”.

00:26:35.789 --> 00:26:40.799
King Egg searched the world for knowledge
on Valyrian dragon-breeding.

00:26:40.799 --> 00:26:46.649
But we don’t have to go to Asshai – cause
we can learn knowledge and skills on Skillshare.

00:26:46.649 --> 00:26:50.840
Skillshare is an online learning site with
thousands of classes in art, design, business,

00:26:50.840 --> 00:26:56.830
and even cooking eggs.. with fire – no human
sacrifice required.

00:26:56.830 --> 00:27:01.740
There’re even classes by Kurzgesagt on video
editing in After Effects, which is what we

00:27:01.740 --> 00:27:02.740
use.

00:27:02.740 --> 00:27:04.419
There’s some really good stuff here.

00:27:04.419 --> 00:27:08.880
And the first thousand people to click the
link below can get a free trial of Skillshare

00:27:08.880 --> 00:27:09.880
Premium.

00:27:09.880 --> 00:27:14.860
After the trial, it’s less than ten bucks
a month for access to all these classes.

00:27:14.860 --> 00:27:20.190
So learn something new, and help Alt Shift
X, by trying Skillshare.

00:27:20.190 --> 00:27:21.440
Thanks for watching.

00:27:21.440 --> 00:27:23.970
Links to the artists and references are below.

00:27:23.970 --> 00:27:31.559
Thanks to Patrons Cami Hunt, Kyle Lim, mario_incandenza,
(at)Surdo, Blake Dale, Ashik Ishtiak, Harith

00:27:31.559 --> 00:27:35.149
Muthanna Alqurtass, and Bambuslocke.

00:27:35.149 --> 00:27:37.500
Cheers.

00:27:37.500 --> 00:27:41.640
If nothing else, the tragedy of Summerhall
is a good example of why you should never

00:27:41.640 --> 00:27:44.109
bring high explosives to a baby shower.

